<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμήχαν-ος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμάχ</span>- [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾱ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, <i>skilful in contriving,
				inventive</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμήχανος</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				381
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				344d
			</span></i>, etc.: c. gen., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμήχανος λόγου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					408b
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλίων εὐ. ἔργων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					4.593
				</span></i>
			: with a Prep., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. πρὸς τὸν
			βίον</span>, of birds, <i>full of devices</i> for supporting
			life, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				614b34
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				616b34
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, of the bee, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				15.3.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔν τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					20.92
				</span></i>
			: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὐ</span>., =
			foreg., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.830c
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.170
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristaenet.
				2.15
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, of things, <i>skilfully contrived, ingenious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τῶν ἀμηχάνων πόρους εὐμηχάνους
					πορίζων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					759
				</span></i>
			 (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος πορίζειν</span> Bentl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίνοιαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					600a
				</span></i>
			.</div>
